-- title:
--   Prime support of a paired divisor least common multiple
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be a finite index set, $R$ a natural number, and $z:\kappa\to\mathbb N\times\mathbb N$ an admissible smooth divisor-family choice at scale $R$. Suppose $z$ is squarefree as a paired divisor choice. Every prime factor of its paired-divisor least common multiple is at most $R$:
--   $$
--   \operatorname{PrimeFactors}(\operatorname{lcm}_{\mathrm{pair}}(z))
--   \subseteq\{p:p\text{ is prime and }p\le R\}.
--   $$
